   "id": "t91",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 140,
   "y": 1565.75,
   "width": 538.1,
   "height": 23.75,
   "text": "4  \u00b7  _yen  \u2014  the k shortest loopless routes",
   "originalText": "4  \u00b7  _yen  \u2014  the k shortest loopless routes",
   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 17,
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 554646833,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 20562661,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1700000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "id": "t92",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 144,
   "y": 1613.75,
   "width": 547.0,
   "height": 265.625,
   "text": "One route is not enough \u2014 we want several so the fleet can spread out.\nYen returns the  k  shortest routes that never repeat a zone, cheapest first.\n\nfound        routes locked in     \u2192 starts as [ Dijkstra shortest ]\ncandidates   heap of next options \u2192 keyed by _turns(route), then a counter\n\nrepeat until  found  has  k  routes (or we run dry):\n  previous = last route locked in\n  for each position  i  along  previous :\n    root     = previous[:i+1]       shared prefix, ends at 'spur node'\n    cut_here = edges a found route already took after this same root\n               \u2192 ban them, forcing the spur to diverge here\n    also ban root's earlier nodes \u2192 no looping back\n    spur     = _dijkstra(spur node \u2192 end)  with those bans\n    whole    = root[:-1] + spur     prefix + fresh tail\n    if new \u2192 push  whole  onto  candidates\n  pop the cheapest candidate \u2192 append to  found",
   "originalText": "One route is not enough \u2014 we want several so the fleet can spread out.\nYen returns the  k  shortest routes that never repeat a zone, cheapest first.\n\nfound        routes locked in     \u2192 starts as [ Dijkstra shortest ]\ncandidates   heap of next options \u2192 keyed by _turns(route), then a counter\n\nrepeat until  found  has  k  routes (or we run dry):\n  previous = last route locked in\n  for each position  i  along  previous :\n    root     = previous[:i+1]       shared prefix, ends at 'spur node'\n    cut_here = edges a found route already took after this same root\n               \u2192 ban them, forcing the spur to diverge here\n    also ban root's earlier nodes \u2192 no looping back\n    spur     = _dijkstra(spur node \u2192 end)  with those bans\n    whole    = root[:-1] + spur     prefix + fresh tail\n    if new \u2192 push  whole  onto  candidates\n  pop the cheapest candidate \u2192 append to  found",
   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 11,
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
