   "id": "t132",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 140,
   "y": 2700.5,
   "width": 667.68,
   "height": 23.75,
   "text": "6  \u00b7  plan()  +  _best_next_route  \u2014  simulate-and-place",
   "originalText": "6  \u00b7  plan()  +  _best_next_route  \u2014  simulate-and-place",
   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 17,
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1201230074,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1403396873,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1700000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "id": "t133",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 144,
   "y": 2748.5,
   "width": 526.0,
   "height": 296.875,
   "text": "Now we hold a small set of SAFE candidate routes. Which one per drone?\nPlace drones one at a time. For each new drone, try it on every candidate,\nactually replay the fleet, and keep the route it lands earliest on.\n\ntrial   = (plan so far + [route])   last _TRIAL_WINDOW (20) drones only\narrival = Simulation(graph, trial).arrival_of_last()\n          \u2192 the Simulation replays those drones turn by turn and\n            returns the turn this newest drone reaches the end\n            (an oracle \u2014 the planner re-implements no movement rule)\n          \u2192 a RuntimeError = this route jams the fleet \u2192 skip it\n\nwhy it works\n  \u2022 short routes fill first (they arrive soonest)\n  \u2022 once a short route clogs, a longer parallel route wins \u2014\n    so the fleet spreads by itself\n  \u2022 replaying only the last 20 drones keeps planning\n    O(drones \u00b7 k \u00b7 window \u00b7 turns)  \u2014 linear in fleet size\n  \u2022 spreading across parallel restricted corridors is what\n    beats the challenger record  (43 < 45 turns)",
   "originalText": "Now we hold a small set of SAFE candidate routes. Which one per drone?\nPlace drones one at a time. For each new drone, try it on every candidate,\nactually replay the fleet, and keep the route it lands earliest on.\n\ntrial   = (plan so far + [route])   last _TRIAL_WINDOW (20) drones only\narrival = Simulation(graph, trial).arrival_of_last()\n          \u2192 the Simulation replays those drones turn by turn and\n            returns the turn this newest drone reaches the end\n            (an oracle \u2014 the planner re-implements no movement rule)\n          \u2192 a RuntimeError = this route jams the fleet \u2192 skip it\n\nwhy it works\n  \u2022 short routes fill first (they arrive soonest)\n  \u2022 once a short route clogs, a longer parallel route wins \u2014\n    so the fleet spreads by itself\n  \u2022 replaying only the last 20 drones keeps planning\n    O(drones \u00b7 k \u00b7 window \u00b7 turns)  \u2014 linear in fleet size\n  \u2022 spreading across parallel restricted corridors is what\n    beats the challenger record  (43 < 45 turns)",
   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "baseline": 11,
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#adb5bd",
   "backgroundColor": "#f1f3f5",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   },
   "seed": 1830514796,
   "version": 1,
